  "comments": "One year after the &quot;Mob of Roos&quot; was introduced into circulation to replace the Dollar Note the obverse of the coin was changed from Arnold Machin&#039;s second portrait design to Raphael David Maklouf&#039;s third portrait design. This obverse was in use on the MOR coin from 1985 until 1998. in 1999 the Ian Rank Broadley fourth portrait was introduced to the MOR coin.<br /><br />\r\nIn 1992 a Re-issue of the 1985 coin was released in a five-coin set with four other coins unique to the 25mm $1 coin denomination from 1984 to 1992 all with original dates.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5dd688ccea7e9.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5dd688ccea7e9.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"139\" /></a> <a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5dd688d730cf6.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5dd688d730cf6.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"139\" /></a><br /><br />\r\nAccording to the RAM Website 8,000 MOR coins were minted in 1992. This is believed to be a mistake.<br />\r\nHowever some were produced as these pictures prove. One member on Numista has this coin.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5e9ed7fe36c52.png\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5e9ed7fe36c52.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"141\" height=\"250\" /></a> <a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5e9ed8164ffa8.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5e9ed8164ffa8.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"140\" height=\"249\" /></a><br /><br />\r\n&nbsp;This coin type was also issued as a Sterling Silver (.925) version in the 1990 Masterpieces in Silver Proof Sets. (See Link)",
